<article class="env-lemma" id="0C3D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C3D">Lemma <span data-tag="0C3D">31.9.1</span>.</a> Let $f : T \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module. Then $f^{-1}\text{Fit}_ i(\mathcal{F}) \cdot \mathcal{O}_ T = \text{Fit}_ i(f^*\mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZA" data-tag="07ZA">15.8.4</a> part (3). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>